xist yet the  only people that are coming to the  forefront of those with a great deal of  either economic or political baggage  with titles of corruption added to it  that the people are very aware of why  are these technocrats not you might say  visible to the public at large or why  are they not coming forward is there a  reason for that well a huge brain drain  over the past few years many of those  people have left the country there's  just not that much interest in them  coming back and taking part in the  political process but this is one of the  main problems that this president is  facing and that led to his resignation  because the protesters the other  political parties they wanted a  candidate to replace other of the nation  who wasn't part of the political process  and that is something that is very hard  to find I would say virtually impossible  you have to really bring somebody in  from outside of Iraq is that what you  wanted to do and that on its own  proposes a series of challenges under  these circumstances I think this is one  of the major issues that the protesters  were adamant about they wanted somebody  who wasn't establishment in the country  that they didn't have a candidate either  so it wasn't like there was another  option and this is what was the most  difficult point for the president and  this is I believe one of the reasons I'm  led to him being forced to resign  because he was under tremendous pressure  to accept one of these candidates there  was three candidates over the past week  that would put to him by Albin our  coalition and Parliament's and susan's  accept any of them who said he would not  could that mean Ford and announced that  those names and candidates as the next  prime minister because he knew that the  people on the streets would not accept  that and that would mean further unrest  and insecurity it would be unleashed  across the country  so I think he just at this point felt  that he had no other option to resign  